d3d11: tessellation mesh grid for every patch of a threadgroup

Applies on top of 0015.

The vertex-hull object function runs patch_per_group patches per
threadgroup, and every patch appends its mesh workloads to one counter
that sizes the mesh grid.  Two defects made tessellated draws flicker
from frame to frame (Unigine Heaven 4.0 DX11, tessellation Normal: the
bridge after the cannon and the dark corridor; tessellation off was
clean, fullscreen was broken too):

- The grid limit (air.max_mesh_work_groups) was one patch's maximum
  workload count, while a threadgroup dispatches up to patch_per_group
  times as many.  Dispatching past the declared limit is undefined.
  The limit is now max_workload_count * patch_per_group, which the
  payload's workload array was already sized for.
- Each patch's first thread cleared the shared counter before adding its
  own workloads (clearing what other patches had already counted), and
  the dispatching thread read it with no barrier after the other patches'
  appends.  The counter is now zeroed once before the barrier that ends
  the vertex zone, and the dispatch reads it after a barrier every
  thread reaches.

Both defects are real by construction, but this patch does NOT fix the
visible Heaven corruption: one clean run by eye was luck.  A frame-diff
detector (transient A->B->A frames per 20x20 block of the window
recording) counts 100+ broken frames over the bridge scene with and
without this patch, on a natural demo run (no key pressed); tessellation
off and all tessellated draws skipped both count 0 (2026-10-02).

The vertex-hull variant digest takes a constant, so conversions cached
by an earlier build are not replayed.

